# Local Vite proxy target; on Vercel this is a SERVER-SIDE function variable.
# On Vercel use the hosted Express HTTPS origin, without /api.
API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000
# Public Socket.IO backend origin. Blank locally; hosted backend HTTPS origin on Vercel.
VITE_REALTIME_URL=
# On Vercel serverless backends, leave blank or use disabled; notifications poll.
# Only set an HTTPS origin when that backend runs a persistent Socket.IO server.
# The original application always uses the backend; no standalone demo mode.
# Never put database credentials or provider keys in VITE_* variables.
# This SAME frontend includes buyer, farmer, and operations/admin portals.
# Admin entry: /login/operations. No separate admin build is required.
# Vercel: set these in Project Settings > Environment Variables, then redeploy.
# Production example:
# API_URL=https://your-api.onrender.com
# VITE_REALTIME_URL=https://your-api.onrender.com
# Build: npm ci, then npm run build; output: dist; Node: 24.x.
# Root: agrilink/client. Enable inclusion of source files outside the root.
